BTW In classic C you ~often~ sometimes write:
(edit: Well you often write `do/while(0)` macros, but breaks are not as common. They're useful regardless though.)

```cpp
do {
    if (...) break;
    if (...) break;
    if (...) break;
    do_something();
} while (0)
```

It would allow you to prevent the repeated COM calls and reduce the line width.
